    <section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="changes-heading"><h2 id="changes-heading" class="section-title">How changes are detected and reviewed</h2><p class="prose-policy mt-2">Maintainers and contributors monitor official journals, legislature and regulator websites, consultation portals and government press releases for the covered jurisdictions. Each development is recorded as a change event with its date, source, practical impact and impact level (urgent, high, routine), then reviewed before publication. Records affected by a change are re-verified and their content version incremented. The <a href="{{ route('changes.index') }}">change log</a> and its RSS feed are the public record of this process; the repository history shows every edit.</p></section>

    <section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="limits-heading"><h2 id="limits-heading" class="section-title">Known limitations</h2><ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-brand-body"><li>Coverage is deliberately narrow and deep: a small number of jurisdictions with structured records rather than a broad but shallow list.</li><li>Many records are still pending human verification; the verification line on each page tells you which.</li><li>Some official documents are available only in local languages or without stable URLs; such records say so in their source reference.</li><li>Framework mappings to ISO/IEC 42001 and the NIST AI RMF are original editorial judgements with stated confidence, not official crosswalks.</li><li>Application dates can change after enactment; a record is only as current as its last verification.</li></ul></section>

    <section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="ai-heading"><h2 id="ai-heading" class="section-title">Disclosure of AI assistance</h2><p class="prose-policy mt-2">AI tools may be used to help draft summaries, structure records and detect changes. Every published record must still link to an official source and pass human review before it is marked verified; AI output is never published as verified fact on its own. The initial dataset was drafted with AI assistance and is labelled "pending review" until reviewers complete verification.</p></section>
